<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  OBD Platform - Phase E: the platform's outbound dialplan.

  WHY THIS FILE REPLACES THE STOCK public.xml
  ============================================

  The stock context answers EVERY extension in 1000-1019 locally with the
  voicemail application, creating two loopback channels:

      <extension name="local_extension">
        <condition field="destination_number" expression="^(10[01][0-9])$">
          <action application="voicemail" data="default"/>

  That produced a FALSE POSITIVE that cost this phase real time, so it is
  recorded rather than quietly fixed.

  The platform switch reported a clean CHANNEL_ANSWER for
  sofia/gateway/local-endpoint-1002/1002 while the test endpoint had no channel
  at all, no SDP had been exchanged (rtp_remote_sdp_str = _undef_), and the
  endpoint's UDP counters had not moved. The switch was answering its OWN
  loopback, not placing a call. The only traces were two loopback channels
  named voicemail-a / voicemail-b, which are easy to miss because the
  channel event for the *originated* leg looks entirely normal.

  The lesson, which is the reason this file is explicit rather than inherited:

      A channel event reports what the LOCAL switch believes. Only the peer's
      own state can confirm a call happened somewhere.

  A local switch that answers its own dialstring will report success for any
  dialstring it has a pattern for. Voicemail answering 1002 is exactly that.

  WHAT THIS DIALPLAN DOES INSTEAD
  ================================

  For an extension that is REGISTERED, bridge the call to the contact that
  registered. No local answer, no loopback, no voicemail. If the extension is
  not registered the call is rejected with USER_NOT_EXISTING, which is a true
  statement, rather than answered by a local application.

  Why bridge-to-registration rather than an explicit address: measured on this
  build, mod_sofia routes outbound SIP BY DOMAIN against the registration
  database of the profile it originates from. Every direct-address form fails,
  on either profile, by IP or by DNS name:

      sofia/external/1002@172.25.0.4:5060     -> NO_ROUTE_DESTINATION
      sofia/internal/1002@172.25.0.4:5060     -> NO_ROUTE_DESTINATION
      sofia/external/1002@endpoint-b:5060      -> NO_ROUTE_DESTINATION

  while the domain-qualified form resolves through the registration and works.
  So the contact in the registration database is the ONLY route to the
  endpoint, and hard-coding the endpoint's address would be both wrong and
  fragile (that address is not stable across container recreates).

  SCOPE AND SAFETY
  ===============

  This is a development-environment dialplan for a private Docker network. It
  exposes no service, opens no port, and is not deployed anywhere a carrier or
  a real subscriber exists. It replaces voicemail answering with routing, which
  is what a platform that originates calls needs and what voicemail answering
  actively prevents.
-->
<context name="public">

  <!--
    A registered test extension. Bridge to its registered contact.

    ${destination_number} is used rather than ${sip_destination_user} for the
    same reason the endpoint's dialplan was corrected in Phase E: for a
    gateway-originated call these two differ, and destination_number is the
    number actually dialled.
  -->
  <extension name="obd-bridge-registered-extension">
    <condition field="${sip_destination_user}" expression="^\d{4}$"/>

    <!--
      Reject an extension that never registered, rather than answering it.
      A registered extension is proven to exist; an unregistered one must not
      be answered by anything local.
    -->
    <condition field="${user_exists(sip_destination_user)}" expression="true">
      <action application="set" data="ignore_early_media=true"/>

      <!--
        Bridge to the contact, in the same profile the registration lives in.
        The endpoint registers to the internal profile, so this is the
        internal profile: its database is what holds the contact.
      -->
      <action application="bridge"
              data="sofia/internal/${destination_number}@${domain}"/>
    </condition>

    <!--
      Not registered. USER_NOT_EXISTING is an honest answer; the stock
      voicemail answer was not.
    -->
    <condition field="${user_exists(sip_destination_user)}" expression="false">
      <action application="respond" data="404 Not Found"/>
      <action application="hangup"/>
    </condition>
  </extension>

</context>
